cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Tri-Net v2: a reproducible deep-learning framework for Mpox skin-lesion diagnosis"
version: 0.9.0
date-released: 2026-07-10
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Sudharsanselvaraj/Synergistic-Deep-Learning-for-Monkeypox-Diagnosis"
authors:
  - family-names: "S"
    given-names: "Sudharsan"
keywords:
  - deep-learning
  - medical-imaging
  - monkeypox
  - dermatology
  - ensemble-learning
  - feature-fusion
abstract: >-
  Tri-Net v2 is a leakage-free, reproducible benchmark and library for Mpox skin-lesion
  diagnosis. It combines modern CNN backbones (ConvNeXt, EfficientNetV2, DenseNet,
  InceptionResNetV2) with learned feature fusion, and reports two clearly separated tasks:
  14-class fine-grained diagnosis and binary Mpox screening, with an honest evaluation
  suite (cross-validation, McNemar, Cohen's Kappa, ensemble diversity, Grad-CAM).
